# Agent environment -- copy to .env in this same directory and edit.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#   chmod 600 .env
#
# Every variable below is REQUIRED. There are no defaults -- the
# runtime fails fast at tick start if anything is missing. This is
# intentional: each value is a decision worth making explicitly,
# and silent defaults rot.
#
# bin/tick.sh sources .env from $AGENT_HOME (the repo root) on every
# run. Same file is used for local dev and systemd-managed installs.

# Anthropic API key (NOT the Claude Max OAuth token).
#
# Create in the Anthropic Console (https://console.anthropic.com).
# Use a dedicated key for the agent so usage is itemized separately
# from any other tooling. Set a hard spending limit on the key so a
# pathological tick can't drain the account.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Model used for every agentic tick. Pin a specific model ID rather
# than an alias so version drift doesn't surprise the harness.
#
# Sensible choices:
#   claude-sonnet-4-6           # balanced cost/capability -- the working default
#   claude-opus-4-7             # premium -- complex reasoning, ambiguous tasks
#   claude-haiku-4-5-20251001   # cheap/fast -- light tasks only
AGENT_MODEL=

# Model for in-harness "thinking" tasks (commit-subject derivation,
# post-shape decisions, reflection passes). These are single-shot
# direct API calls (no tool use, no agentic loop), so Haiku is
# usually the right pick -- cheap and fast enough.
AGENT_MODEL_THINKING=

# Forgejo instance the agent works against.
FORGEJO_URL=

# Bot user's API token. The bot's identity is derived from this token
# (GET /api/v1/user). Required scopes:
#   read:user        -- whoami
#   write:repository -- repo content reads, PR listing/creation
#   write:issue      -- issue create/comment/label/assign/close
# (Forgejo splits repository and issue scopes -- you need both.)
# Push access for git is via the SSH key, separate from API scopes.
FORGEJO_TOKEN=

# SSH endpoint used for clone-on-demand. Format is "host" (port 22)
# or "host:port" (explicit). Examples:
#   FORGEJO_HOST=git.example.com           # port 22
#   FORGEJO_HOST=git.example.com:22381     # custom port
FORGEJO_HOST=

# Forgejo username to assign each PR to for human review. The agent
# opens PRs assigned to this user, and picks back up any PRs that
# get reassigned to him on subsequent ticks (the "assignment dance"
# -- review comments come in via reassignment, agent addresses and
# reassigns back).
FORGEJO_REVIEWER=

# Per-tick Claude timeout (passed to `timeout`). Format: "60m",
# "30m", "2h". The whole tick (Claude invocation + post-processing)
# is bounded by this; pick something generous enough that real work
# doesn't get killed mid-flight, but tight enough that a wedged
# process doesn't burn the next tick's slot.
TICK_TIMEOUT=

# How many days back the harness looks when summarizing recent
# activity for context (commit log + merged-PR review threads
# surfaced inline in user messages). 30 is a reasonable starting
# point.
AGENT_RECALL_DAYS=

# Bot's website repo, format <owner>/<repo>. Opt-in -- leave
# unset to disable all website work (reading pipeline + site-work
# block both no-op without it). When set, the harness clones the
# repo on first need and runs the reading pipeline + site-work
# block during the shift window when no claimable issue is found.
WEBSITE_REPO=

# =====================================================================
# Email delivery (SMTP2GO) -- SHARED by every opt-in report subsystem
# below (SEO, market). Set these once and any report that's also
# configured can deliver. SMTP2GO_API_KEY is a v3 API key; SMTP2GO_SENDER
# is the verified From: address reports are sent from. Leave unset to
# disable all email-delivering subsystems.
# =====================================================================
SMTP2GO_API_KEY=
SMTP2GO_SENDER=

# =====================================================================
# SEO analysis pass -- OPT-IN. Everything below is optional; unlike the
# required block at the top, the SEO pass no-ops cleanly when these are
# unset. It enumerates Google Search Console domain properties weekly
# (one per tick), emails a graded report (via the SMTP2GO block above),
# and -- for sites you mark agentic -- files a Forgejo ticket the normal
# work flow picks up once that repo passes validation. Read-only by
# default; no LLM (scripted analysis).
# =====================================================================

# Google Search Console OAuth (refresh-token flow). Create an OAuth
# "Desktop app" client in Google Cloud, then mint the refresh token
# once with `bin/gsc-auth.sh` (run it locally -- it needs a browser).
# Access tokens are derived at runtime and never stored. Scope used:
# webmasters.readonly. Leave all three unset to disable the SEO pass.
GSC_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=
GSC_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=
GSC_OAUTH_REFRESH_TOKEN=

# Routing. SEO_PRIMARY_EMAIL receives a report for EVERY domain (the
# SEO-system inbox) -- required. SEO_EXTRA_RECIPIENTS adds selective
# recipients per site, grammar "email=site1,site2|email2=site3" (pipe
# between people, comma between their sites). Primary is always copied,
# so no separate CC is needed.
SEO_PRIMARY_EMAIL=
SEO_EXTRA_RECIPIENTS=

# Agentic sites: domains where Igor should also file a ticket (and, once
# the repo validates, do the work). Grammar "domain=owner/repo|domain2=
# owner/repo2". The mapped repo must be a bot-accessible Forgejo repo.
# Domains not listed here are report-only (email, no ticket).
SEO_AGENTIC_SITES=

# Volume knobs (optional; sensible defaults shown). SEO_IMPRESSION_FLOOR
# drops queries/pages below N impressions over the 28-day window before
# ranking. SEO_TOP_K caps how many items per analysis type surface in
# the email/ticket. Don't tune these off the first pass -- the cold-start
# backlog looks heavier than steady state; give it 2-3 weekly cycles.
SEO_IMPRESSION_FLOOR=50
SEO_TOP_K=10

# Debug/isolation: when set to a single bare domain (e.g.
# joshtronic.com), the SEO pass runs ONLY that domain and skips the full
# GSC enumeration -- everything else behaves like a normal day (it still
# emails, files any agentic ticket, records opportunities, and stamps the
# domain done for the week). Use it to smoke-test one site before the
# full sweep. To re-run, clear the domain's weekly stamp under .seo in
# ~/.local/state/agent/discretionary-state.json. Leave unset for
# production (the full sweep).
SEO_DEBUG_DOMAIN=

# =====================================================================
# Market report -- OPT-IN. A daily (Mon-Fri) email of the previous
# trading day's prices (company, high, low, close, volume) for a fixed
# set of symbols, via the marketstack v2 EOD API. Scripted (no LLM),
# email-only; delivers
# through the SMTP2GO block above. Sends on the first weekday tick after
# midnight (no send-time knob -- midnight is the day rollover, same as
# the rest of the harness). No-ops cleanly on weekends, once the day's
# already sent, or when anything below is unset.
# =====================================================================

# marketstack API key. Create one at https://marketstack.com. The key is
# passed as a query-string parameter; on a paid plan the default base URL
# is HTTPS (encrypted in transit). Leave unset to disable the report.
MARKETSTACK_API_KEY=

# Symbols to report, comma-separated tickers (e.g. AAPL,MSFT,TSLA). All
# are fetched in a single marketstack request.
MARKET_SYMBOLS=

# Recipients, comma-separated email addresses. One report goes to the
# whole list (a flat list -- this report is intentionally single, not
# per-symbol routed).
MARKET_RECIPIENTS=

# Optional base URL override. Defaults to the paid HTTPS v2 host
# (https://api.marketstack.com/v2). Set to the free-tier HTTP host only
# if you must -- the API key then crosses the wire in plaintext. No
# trailing slash.
# MARKETSTACK_BASE_URL=https://api.marketstack.com/v2
